 Let $x > y > z > 0$.  We have $\left((x - y) + (y - z) + z\right)\left(\frac{1}{x - y} + \frac{1}{y - z} + \frac{1}{z}\right) = 1 + \frac{x - y}{y - z} + \frac{x - y}{z} + \frac{y - z}{x - y} + \frac{z}{x - y} + \frac{z}{y - z} + \frac{x}{z} \ge 7$  by Cauchy Schwarz.  Hence,
\begin{align*}
x + \frac{108}{(x - y)^3 (y - z)^2 z} &= \left((x - y) + (y - z) + z\right) \cdot \frac{108}{72\left((x - y)^3 (y - z)^2 z\right)} \left(\frac{1}{x - y} + \frac{1}{y - z} + \frac{1}{z}\right)^3 \\
&\ge \frac{49}{3},
\end{align*}
with equality when $x - y = y - z = z = \frac{x}{3}$, or $x = 3y = 9z$.  Therefore, the minimum value is $\boxed{\frac{49}{3}}$.</think> <answer> $\frac{49}{3}$ </answer>

 Let $x > y > z > 0$.  Notice that
\begin{align*}
x &= \frac{x - y + y - z + z}{3} \cdot 3, \\
\frac{1}{(x - y)^3 (y - z)^2 z} &= \frac{1}{\left(\frac{x - y}{3}\right)^3 \left(\frac{y - z}{3}\right)^2 \cdot 3z}.
\end{align*}
By AM-GM Inequality,
\begin{align*}
x + \frac{108}{(x - y)^3 (y - z)^2 z}
&= \frac{x - y + y - z + z}{3} \cdot 3 + \frac{108}{\left(\frac{x - y}{3}\right)^3 \left(\frac{y - z}{3}\right)^2 \cdot 3z} \\
&\ge 6 \sqrt[6]{\frac{x - y}{3} \cdot \frac{x - y}{3} \cdot \frac{x - y}{3} \cdot \frac{y - z}{3} \cdot \frac{y - z}{3} \cdot 3z} \cdot 3 + \frac{108}{\left(\frac{x - y}{3}\right)^3 \left(\frac{y - z}{3}\right)^2 \cdot 3z} \\
&= 6 \cdot 3 + \frac{108}{\left(\frac{x - y}{3}\right)^3 \left(\frac{y - z}{3}\right)^2 \cdot 3z} \\
&= 18 + \frac{108}{\left(\frac{x - y}{3}\right)^3 \left(\frac{y - z}{3}\right)^2 \cdot 3z}.
\end{align*}
When the equality holds, $x - y = y - z = 3z$, which implies $x = 5z$ and $y = 4z$. Thus, the minimum value is $\boxed{18}$.
